
9. Jenkinsfile Structure

A Jenkins pipeline is usually stored in:

Project Root
    |
    |-- Jenkinsfile

Example:

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo 'Build'
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                echo 'Test'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                echo 'Deploy'
            }
        }
    }
}
10. Parameters

Parameters allow user input before starting a build.

Example:

parameters {
    string(
        name: 'VERSION',
        defaultValue: '1.0'
    )
}

User enters:

VERSION = 2.0
11. Environment Variables

Used to store values.

Example:

environment {
    APP_NAME = "BankApp"
}

Use:

echo "${APP_NAME}"
12. Jenkins Multi-Branch Pipelines

Automatically creates pipelines for Git branches.

Example:

main
develop
feature/login
feature/payment

Jenkins builds each branch separately.

Benefits:

Branch isolation
Easy testing
Better CI process
13. Pipeline Stages
Stage 1: Checkout Code

Download code from GitHub.

git 'https://github.com/user/project.git'
Stage 2: Build

Compile code.

Example:

sh 'mvn clean compile'
Stage 3: Test

Run tests.

sh 'mvn test'
Stage 4: Package

Create JAR/WAR file.

sh 'mvn package'
Stage 5: Deploy

Deploy application.

echo 'Deploying'
Post Actions

Run after pipeline finishes.

post {
    success {
        echo 'Success'
    }

    failure {
        echo 'Failed'
    }
}
